1| # Error handling
2| 
3| > Consumer guidance. For internal error architecture see [Error Architecture](./errors.md).
4| 
5| All public client packages normalize transport failures into structured platform errors.
6| 
7| ## Typed error discrimination
8| 
9| Consumers should switch on `err.kind` rather than `instanceof` chains or message parsing. Every error thrown from the public API surface is a `GoodVibesError` with a stable `kind` discriminant.
10| 
11| ```ts
12| import { GoodVibesError } from '@goodvibes-jev/engine/platform/errors';
13| 
14| try {
15|   await platformClient.operator.control.snapshot();
16| } catch (err) {
17|   if (err instanceof GoodVibesError) {
18|     switch (err.kind) {
19|       case 'auth':
20|         // Redirect to login or surface auth UI
21|         break;
22|       case 'rate-limit':
23|         // Wait retryAfterMs then retry
24|         await delay(err.retryAfterMs ?? 1000);
25|         break;
26|       case 'network':
27|       case 'service':
28|         if (err.recoverable) {
29|           // Retry with backoff
30|         }
31|         break;
32|       case 'config':
33|         // Fix platform initialization options, do not retry
34|         break;
35|       case 'contract':
36|       case 'protocol':
37|       case 'internal':
38|       case 'tool':
39|       case 'validation':
40|       case 'not-found':
41|       case 'unknown':
42|         // Log and surface to the user
43|         break;
44|     }
45|   } else {
46|     throw err;
47|   }
48| }
49| ```
50| 
51| See [error-kinds.md](./error-kinds.md) for the full reference on each kind.
52| 
53| ## TUI and consumer example
54| 
55| ```ts
56| import type { GoodVibesPlatform } from '@goodvibes-jev/engine/platform';
57| import { GoodVibesError } from '@goodvibes-jev/engine/platform/errors';
58| import type { OperatorMethodOutput } from '@goodvibes-jev/engine/platform/contracts';
59| 
60| async function safeSnapshot(platformClient: GoodVibesPlatform): Promise<OperatorMethodOutput<'control.snapshot'> | null> {
61|   try {
62|     return await platformClient.operator.control.snapshot();
63|   } catch (err) {
64|     if (!(err instanceof GoodVibesError)) throw err;
65|     if (err.kind === 'auth') {
66|       // surface login prompt in TUI
67|       return null;
68|     }
69|     if (err.kind === 'network' && err.recoverable) {
70|       // schedule reconnect
71|       return null;
72|     }
73|     throw err;
74|   }
75| }
76| ```
77| 
78| ## Class-specific handling
79| 
80| The `HttpStatusError`, `ConfigurationError`, and `ContractError` subclasses remain available when callers need class-specific handling. Prefer `err.kind` for broad control flow.
81| 
82| ```ts
83| import { HttpStatusError } from '@goodvibes-jev/engine/platform/errors';
84| 
85| try {
86|   await platformClient.operator.accounts.snapshot();
87| } catch (error) {
88|   if (error instanceof HttpStatusError) {
89|     if (error.status === 401) {
90|       // redirect to login, refresh token, or surface auth UI
91|     }
92|     console.error(error.status, error.category, error.hint);
93|   }
94|   throw error;
95| }
96| ```
97| 
98| ## Useful fields
99| 
100| Every error exposes the full set of 18 structured fields. See the canonical [Useful fields on every `GoodVibesError`](./error-kinds.md#useful-fields-on-every-goodvibeserror) table for the complete list and types.
101| 
102| Do not parse `message` strings when the structured fields are available.
103| 
104| ## Core error classes
105| 
106| Four classes cover everything the platform throws; the three specialized classes
107| extend the base, so an `instanceof GoodVibesError` check catches them all.
108| 
109| | Class | When you get it |
110| | --- | --- |
111| | `GoodVibesError` | The base class for every platform error; carries the structured fields above |
112| | `ConfigurationError` | The platform was constructed or configured incorrectly (`ENGINE_CONFIGURATION_ERROR`, kind `config`) |
113| | `ContractError` | Client and daemon disagree about the contract (`ENGINE_CONTRACT_ERROR`, kind `contract`) |
114| | `HttpStatusError` | An HTTP failure with no more specific mapping (`ENGINE_HTTP_STATUS_ERROR`, source `transport`) |
115| 
116| ## Category guidance
117| 
118| `ErrorCategory` has 16 values: the 15 daemon wire categories plus `contract`, which is added by the platform and is never marshalled over the wire.
119| 
120| - `authentication`
121|   Missing or invalid credentials.
122| - `authorization`
123|   Valid credentials, insufficient scopes/roles.
124| - `billing`
125|   Payment required or quota/billing failure.
126| - `rate_limit`
127|   Retry after backoff.
128| - `timeout`
129|   Remote timeout or transport timeout.
130| - `network`
131|   Connectivity failure before a response was received.
132| - `bad_request`
133|   Malformed or schema-invalid request payload.
134| - `not_found`
135|   Remote resource does not exist.
136| - `permission`
137|   Operation denied due to insufficient permissions.
138| - `tool`
139|   Tool execution failure.
140| - `config`
141|   Local platform misconfiguration.
142| - `protocol`
143|   Wire-format or protocol-level failure.
144| - `service`
145|   Remote failure or server instability.
146| - `internal`
147|   Daemon or platform internal failure.
148| - `unknown`
149|   Unclassified error.
150| - `contract`
151|   Contract drift or invalid method/endpoint usage (platform-local; not a wire category).
152|

164| [Voice and Streaming TTS](./voice.md)). A web UI owns local playback. Read the
165| `fetch` response body as a `ReadableStream` and feed it to the Web Audio API or
166| a `MediaSource` so audio starts before the full clip arrives.
167| 
168| ```ts
169| const controller = new AbortController();
170| const res = await fetch(`${baseUrl}/api/voice/tts/stream`, {
171|   method: 'POST',
172|   credentials: 'include',
173|   headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
174|   body: JSON.stringify({ providerId: 'elevenlabs', text: 'Read this aloud' }),
175|   signal: controller.signal,
176| });
177| 
178| if (!res.ok || !res.body) {
179|   throw new Error(`tts/stream failed: ${res.status}`);
180| }
181| 
182| const mediaSource = new MediaSource();
183| const audio = new Audio();
184| audio.src = URL.createObjectURL(mediaSource);
185| 
186| mediaSource.addEventListener('sourceopen', async () => {
187|   const contentType = res.headers.get('content-type') ?? 'audio/mpeg';
188|   const sourceBuffer = mediaSource.addSourceBuffer(contentType);
189|   const reader = res.body!.getReader();
190| 
191|   for (;;) {
192|     const { done, value } = await reader.read();
193|     if (done) break;
194|     await new Promise((resolve) => {
195|       sourceBuffer.addEventListener('updateend', resolve, { once: true });
196|       sourceBuffer.appendBuffer(value);
197|     });
198|   }
199|   mediaSource.endOfStream();
200| });
201| 
202| await audio.play();
203| ```
204| 
205| The `Content-Type` and `X-GoodVibes-Audio-Format` response headers describe the
206| audio encoding; use them to pick the `MediaSource` MIME type or Web Audio decode
207| path. Call `controller.abort()` when the user stops playback so the daemon
208| cancels the upstream provider stream.
209| 
210| ## Error handling
211| 
212| All platform errors extend `GoodVibesError` and expose the same `kind` taxonomy
213| across every browser surface. See
214| [Browser Integration → Error handling](./browser-integration.md#error-handling)
215| for the handling pattern and [Error Kinds](./error-kinds.md) for the full
216| taxonomy.
217| 
218| ## Observability
219| 
220| Observability works from web UI contexts exactly as on the full surface. Import
221| observer helpers from `@goodvibes-jev/engine/platform/observer` so scoped browser bundles
222| stay narrow, and pass `createConsoleObserver()` as the `observer` option when
223| creating the platform. See
224| [Browser Integration → Observability](./browser-integration.md#observability) for
225| the shared example and [Observability](./observability.md) for the full observer
226| API.
